  "hooks": [
    "Jacob preaches reluctantly: it grieves him to be so bold before the wives and children (2:7).",
    "He holds up the Lamanites as the better husbands (3:5–7) — the reversal Helaman later makes national.",
    "The book's longest chapter isn't Jacob's: it is Zenos, a prophet the Bible never mentions.",
    "Sherem demands a sign and gets one (7:13–15). Korihor repeats the pattern in Alma 30.",
    "Jacob signs off with a French word, adieu (7:27) — its only appearance in the Book of Mormon."
  ]
